Connect forging and rolling with deformation fields, heat, and final structure (@metal-forging-rolling: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Principles-of-Metal-Forming-NPTEL.lingua#r_7V0FT0Q67E19BFVTK57QABNPX8", #source "../sources/Ferrous-Metals-Processing-BREF.lingua#r_49RSZE1MH5VHM49SDAXFQGHWRD", #source "../sources/Material-Processing-Theory-and-Practice-NPTEL.lingua#r_7BSA0B8283WGYN6KF2609N2GK2", #source "../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Extrusion-drawing-sheet-formability-and-failure.lingua#r_78H51E21H22BGE65JJNHVR9ASE", #materials-engineering "Extrusion-drawing-sheet-formability-and-failure.lingua#r_78H51E21H22BGE65JJNHVR9ASE") { r_5A8TVVAWFVCYFBPR7Q08V2FEWX
**Read:** [Principles of Metal Forming Technology — Pradeep Kumar Jha, NPTEL](../sources/Principles-of-Metal-Forming-NPTEL.lingua#r_7V0FT0Q67E19BFVTK57QABNPX8), all forging, rolling, analysis, and defect material; [Ferrous Metals Processing Industry — European Commission BREF](../sources/Ferrous-Metals-Processing-BREF.lingua#r_49RSZE1MH5VHM49SDAXFQGHWRD), the whole relevant hot/cold rolling route and utility/surface account; [Material Processing: Metallurgical Aspects, Fundamental and Practical — Dwivedi](../sources/Material-Processing-Theory-and-Practice-NPTEL.lingua#r_7BSA0B8283WGYN6KF2609N2GK2), the entire forging/rolling and material-response sequence; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), complete thermomechanical and structure-evolution discussions used.

Forging and rolling impose spatially varying strain, stress, contact, and thermal histories. Geometry, friction, tool stiffness/condition, flow behavior, speed, and temperature affect load, spread, internal quality, surface, and texture. A nominal reduction or final thickness does not describe the full deformation history.

Derive a representative slab, energy, upper-bound, or other stated analytical model with its assumptions. Compare it with numerical or measured evidence, including boundary/contact treatment and constitutive data. Verify equilibrium, work, units, mesh/time dependence where relevant, and a simpler limiting case.

Connect deformation to recovery/recrystallization, grain/phase evolution, segregation/defect response, cooling, and later heat treatment. A successful shape can still carry an undesirable structure or residual stress. Tooling, lubrication, heating, inspection, maintenance, and usable output belong to the whole production account.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete forging and a complete rolling case with original material, process, and measurement methods. Independently reproduce significant load/work or thermal calculations and compare alternative schedules/contact assumptions against product evidence. Analyze a defect or property discrepancy through competing flow, thermal, and structural interpretations. Defend the preferred process on actual product quality and robustness, not only peak force or nominal throughput.

**Continue:** [Compare extrusion, drawing, and sheet forming through flow, anisotropy, and failure evidence](Extrusion-drawing-sheet-formability-and-failure.lingua#r_78H51E21H22BGE65JJNHVR9ASE).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
